1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:04,650
Before you light a single diya this year, know why.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,928
Five stories. Five lamps. And almost nobody knows all of them.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,144
The first lamp is for a prince.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:23,383
Ram was sent into the forest for 14 years, with Sita, and his brother Lakshman.

5
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,513
There, the demon king Ravana stole Sita away, to Lanka.

6
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:36,773
Ram crossed the sea on a bridge of stones. With Hanuman and an army of monkeys, he fought Ravana, and won.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,940
When Ram came home, it was the darkest night of the month.

8
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,484
So the people of Ayodhya lit a lamp in every window, to light his way.

9
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,150
The second lamp is for a goddess.

10
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:04,150
Long ago, gods and demons churned the cosmic ocean, with a mountain for a rod, and a great serpent for a rope.

11
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:09,122
Out of the waves rose Lakshmi, goddess of wealth and good fortune.

12
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:16,616
So on Diwali night, families clean their homes, open their doors, and light lamps, to welcome her in.

13
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,750
The third lamp is for freedom.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,050
The demon Narakasura had locked 16,000 women in his fortress.

15
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:32,650
Krishna and his queen Satyabhama rode out against him, and set every one of them free.

16
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:37,091
In the south of India, that victory is Deepavali itself.

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,350
The fourth lamp is for a promise.

18
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:47,350
The emperor had imprisoned the sixth Sikh Guru, Guru Hargobind, in Gwalior Fort.

19
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:54,750
When he was freed, he would not leave alone. 52 kings held the tails of his robe, and walked out with him.

20
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,126
Sikhs call it Bandi Chhor Divas, the day of release. And the Golden Temple shines with light.

21
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:06,150
The fifth lamp is for a teacher.

22
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:12,150
On this night, Jains believe, Lord Mahavira attained nirvana at Pavapuri.

23
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:18,169
The great light of knowledge was gone. So people lit small lamps, to keep it with them.

24
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,650
Five stories. Five lamps.

25
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,550
And every one of them ends the same way.

26
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,715
Darkness loses.

27
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:39,983
So this year, when you light your diya, you're lighting all five.

28
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,600
Happy Diwali.
